        "item_0": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What makes GPOD special?",
            "answer": "<p>A cradle-free magnetic head, so your phone snaps on and off one-handed — no clamp to fight, no dropped phone. And a pointed end that stakes straight into the ground and holds, whatever the wind is doing.</p><p>We build each model in the material it actually needs: lightweight carbon fiber on the GPOD and GPOD X, where shaving every ounce matters most, and aircraft-grade aluminum alloy on the Pauly P, Studio 2.0, Travel and Pocket G, where adjustability and all-day durability lead.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which phones work with the magnetic mount?",
            "answer": "<p>All of them. iPhone 12 and newer with MagSafe snap straight on with nothing added. Android phones and older iPhones use the 3M metal plates included with every purchase — stick one on your phone or case and it's just as magnetic.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does it work with a thick case, iPad, or GoPro?",
            "answer": "<p>Thick or non-MagSafe cases: put an included metal plate on the case and you're set. iPads and tablets: yes — our magnets hold devices up to 3.5 lbs (we recommend the Studio 2.0 for larger iPads). GoPro and cameras: every magnetic head has a universal 1/4\" camera thread.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will the magnet hurt my phone or iPad?",
            "answer": "<p>Nope. Our magnetic heads are perfectly safe for phones and tablets.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much does the GPOD weigh? Will it fit in my golf bag?",
            "answer": "<p>The original GPOD weighs about 8 ounces — a sleeve of 6 golf balls. Every monopod is designed to ride in a standard golf bag; the GPOD X collapses to 20 inches specifically for bag carry. Exact lengths and weights are on each product page and the <a href=\"/pages/compare-gpod-models\">compare page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_5": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What does the remote do?",
            "answer": "<p>The Bluetooth remote pairs with your phone in seconds and starts/stops recording from address — no walking back and forth to your camera between swings. Pairing steps are in our <a href=\"/pages/support-guides\">Support &amp; Guides</a> hub.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_6": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What's in the Sportsbox 3D bundle?",
            "answer": "<p>The bundle pairs a GPOD Travel tripod with a full year of Sportsbox 3D — an app that turns your swing videos into 3D body-movement data. Redemption instructions are in <a href=\"/pages/support-guides\">Support &amp; Guides</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_7": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use GPOD for things besides golf?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Customers use GPOD for baseball, football, soccer, hiking, beach days, travel, and content creation of every kind. If you point a camera at it, GPOD can hold the camera.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_8": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use the magnetic head on other tripods?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — the patent-pending magnetic heads have a universal 1/4\" camera thread in the back, so they screw onto any standard tripod or monopod.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_9": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do you ship internationally? How fast?",
            "answer": "<p>We ship worldwide. In-stock orders placed on a business day are packed and shipped within 1 business day; shipping costs are calculated at checkout, and you'll get tracking by text or email.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_10": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is your return policy and warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>If you're not satisfied, we make it right — see <a href=\"/pages/refund-policy\">Shipping &amp; Returns</a> for the full policy. GPODs are guaranteed to last: if something breaks, contact us and we'll repair or replace it, and most small parts (remotes, knobs, magnets) can be replaced individually.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_11": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "My question isn't here — where do I look?",
            "answer": "<p>Setup videos, troubleshooting (including a stuck lower extension), and remote pairing live in <a href=\"/pages/support-guides\">Support &amp; Guides</a>. Not sure which GPOD to buy? <a href=\"/pages/compare-gpod-models\">Compare models</a> or take the <a href=\"/pages/product-finder-quiz\">30-second finder</a>. Anything else: <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\">contact us</a> — we answer fast.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
